{
  "requirement": "A named label carries decoded name parts. An anonymous label carries the hexadecimal identity hash.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub enum Label {\n    Named(Vec<String>),\n    Hash(String),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Label;\nimpl Debug for Label;\nimpl PartialEq for Label;\nimpl Eq for Label;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The obligations are: (1) a named label carries decoded name parts; (2) an anonymous label carries the hexadecimal identity hash; (3) the enum shape is `Named(Vec<String>)` and `Hash(String)`; (4) `Label` implements Clone, Debug, PartialEq and Eq.\n\nThe tests cover them as follows:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/selector.rs#mod[tests]/fn[parses_named_anonymous_and_ordinal_segments]` parses `impl[Thing/Trait%3CT%3E]`. It asserts the label equals `Label::Named(vec![\"Thing\", \"Trait<T>\"])`, so the parts are split and percent-decoded. This covers (1).\n- The same test parses `use@0123456789AB`. It asserts `Label::Hash(\"0123456789ab\")`, a hexadecimal hash. This covers (2).\n- Constructing and matching both variants with those payload types covers (3). The test also builds `Label::Named(vec![\"a/b\", \"c d\"])` and checks the encoded base `impl[a%2Fb/c%20d]`.\n- `assert_eq!` on labels and segments needs PartialEq and Debug. `segments[2].clone()` needs Clone on `Segment`, which derives Clone and so requires `Label: Clone`. These cover (4) for Clone, Debug and PartialEq.\n- Eq has no direct assertion, but `Segment` derives Eq and so needs `Label: Eq`. The implementation derives `Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq` on `Label`. These trait obligations are compile-time facts that the test code exercises, and `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` also compiles the consumer against the public SDK.\n\nI found no unexercised conditional behavior or plausible violation that these tests would accept.",
